The camera trove: a console and a presets page for a USB camera

troves/camera: everything the studio's Pocket 6K Pro reports over USB, a
control for everything it lets us set, and the first operator page, a page of
curated presets that sets the camera with one button and checks it.

- [x] ptp.py: PTP over Windows Portable Devices (no driver, no admin)
- [x] camera.py: one thread owns the camera; console on 127.0.0.1:8790; state/apply/presets verbs
- [x] console.html: every property, grouped, with a control; record with a two-press confirm
- [x] presets.html + presets.yml: four draft presets; apply, read back, say what took
- [x] fcpm camera
- [x] run with the camera unplugged: "not connected", no hang, both pages clean light/dark/phone
- [ ] followed with the camera attached: a control, a preset, the read-back
- [ ] record start/stop (makes a clip; needs a yes)
- [ ] does the ATEM reset values a USB preset sets? (it holds WB, tint, ND, ISO, angle for Camera 4)
